                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Three Digits is a logic puzzle game developed and published by Cleverweek that proves an engaging experience does not require flashy visuals or complicated mechanics. As the follow-up to Two Digits, it expands on the original concept by presenting players with a more demanding series of mathematical puzzles centered on a single objective. Each stage provides a collection of numbers below one thousand, and the task is to divide them into two groups with identical sums. The rules are immediately understandable, but reaching the correct solution becomes increasingly difficult as the game introduces more elaborate numerical combinations. This straightforward design allows the gameplay to focus entirely on critical thinking and logical deduction, creating a rewarding experience for players who enjoy solving carefully designed puzzles.\n\nThe game features 300 handcrafted puzzles divided into 14 themed level sets, giving players a lengthy progression that steadily increases in complexity. Early challenges help establish the core mechanics without overwhelming newcomers, while later puzzles require considerably more planning, patience, and experimentation. Success rarely comes from guesswork alone, as each solution demands careful analysis of how every number contributes to the overall balance. This gradual escalation creates a satisfying learning curve, encouraging players to improve their problem-solving abilities while continually presenting fresh mental obstacles. The result is a puzzle game that respects the player's intelligence and consistently rewards persistence.\n\nOne of the game's strongest additions is its random puzzle mode, which generates an endless supply of new challenges after the main campaign has been completed. This feature significantly extends the game's lifespan by ensuring there is always another puzzle waiting to be solved. Players who enjoy sharpening their logical reasoning can continue testing themselves long after finishing the handcrafted content, making Three Digits more than a one-time experience. Steam Achievements further enhance replayability by providing additional goals for completionists without distracting from the game's primary focus on solving numerical puzzles.\n\nVisually, Three Digits embraces a clean and highly functional presentation that complements its minimalist philosophy. Every element of the interface is designed for readability, allowing players to focus entirely on the puzzle in front of them. The uncluttered menus and intuitive controls make rearranging numbers effortless, preventing unnecessary frustration during more difficult stages. Rather than relying on elaborate graphics or dramatic visual effects, the game succeeds through clarity and efficiency, creating an atmosphere where concentration remains the highest priority. This restrained presentation pairs well with the thoughtful gameplay, offering a calm environment that encourages deliberate thinking instead of rushed decisions.\n\nDespite its strengths, Three Digits is intentionally specialized and may not appeal to every type of player. Those seeking narrative progression, character development, or varied gameplay mechanics may find the experience somewhat repetitive since every challenge revolves around the same core objective. Likewise, players who are less interested in mathematical reasoning or logic-based gameplay could struggle with the increasing difficulty as the puzzles become more demanding. However, for puzzle enthusiasts who appreciate games built around elegant design and intellectual challenge, this focused approach is precisely what makes the experience so compelling.\n\nThree Digits succeeds by taking a simple concept and refining it into an absorbing collection of brainteasers that consistently reward careful analysis and patience. Cleverweek demonstrates that strong puzzle design can stand on its own without unnecessary distractions, delivering hundreds of thoughtfully crafted challenges alongside an endless random mode that greatly enhances replay value. While its niche appeal means it will not satisfy everyone, fans of logic puzzles and numerical problem-solving will find a polished, satisfying, and mentally stimulating experience that remains engaging from beginning to end.\n\nRating: 5/10",
